@startuml
' User order lifecycle - PlantUML sequence diagram
actor User as U
participant Frontend as F
participant Backend as B
participant PaymentProvider as P
database Database as DB
participant EmailService as E
participant Shipper as S
actor Admin as A

== Browsing & Cart ==
U -> F: Browse products, add to cart
F -> DB: upsert cart rows
DB --> F: OK

== Checkout & Order creation ==
U -> F: Checkout (address, phone, payment method)
F -> B: POST /payments/orders {cart, address, phone}
B -> DB: create order (status: pending) + order_items
DB --> B: order row
B -> P: create payment session / intent
P --> B: payment_url / session_id
B --> F: return payment_url
F -> U: redirect to payment provider

== Payment completes at provider ==
U -> P: complete/authorize payment
P -> B: webhook (payment event)
B -> P: verify webhook signature / validate event
P --> B: verification OK

alt payment success
  B -> DB: insert payment row; update order.status = 'paid'
  DB --> B: OK
  B -> E: send order confirmation email
  E --> B: OK
  B -> F: (optional) push realtime update to UI
else payment failed
  B -> DB: update order.status = 'failed'
  B -> E: notify user of failed payment
end

== Fulfillment & Shipping ==
A -> B: admin confirms & processes order
B -> S: create shipment request
S --> B: tracking_id
B -> DB: update order.status = 'shipped' and add tracking
B -> E: send shipment email (with tracking)

== User views orders ==
U -> F: View Orders page
F -> B: GET /orders (authenticated)
B -> DB: SELECT order, order_items, payments, tracking
DB --> B: order data
B --> F: return order details
F --> U: display order + tracking

== Post-delivery: Review/Feedback ==
U -> F: Leave review for product
F -> B: POST /reviews (Authorization: Bearer <token>)
B -> DB: verify user has a PAID order containing product
alt user purchased
  B -> DB: insert product_review
  DB --> B: inserted review
  B --> F: return success
else not purchased
  B --> F: 403 Forbidden (reject review)
end

== Refund / Return (optional) ==
U -> B: Request refund/return
B -> DB: update order.status = 'refund_pending'
B -> P: initiate refund via payment provider
P --> B: refund status (success/failure)
alt refund success
  B -> DB: update order.status = 'refunded'
  B -> E: notify user
else refund failed
  B -> DB: update order.status = 'refund_failed'
  B -> E: notify user
end

note right of B
  Backend uses service-role key to perform sensitive operations
  Webhook verification is required before updating payment/order state
end note

note left of U
  Reviews are accepted only after successful purchase (enforced server-side)
end note
@enduml
